hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1533","I am Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala, and Saeed bin Abdul-Rahman. He said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, who is Ibn Dinar, who said: I heard Kurayb A servant of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: I spent the night at my aunt Maymunah’s, and when some night had passed, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose He was praying, and he came to a hanging vessel, and he performed a light ablution, then he stood up and prayed, so I stood up and performed ablution, and did the same as he did, then I stood up to his left, So he turned me to his right and prayed as long as God wished, then he lay down and slept until he blew, then the muezzin came to him calling him to prayer, so he went out and prayed.” This is the hadith of Abdul-Jabbar. Al-Makhzoumi said: Kurayb, and he said: “So he went out and prayed but did not perform ablution.” He said: He described his ablution, and made it short, and he did not say: a light ablution."
